Apple's extended return policy went into effect today for the 2026 holiday shopping season. The policy applies to most products sold by Apple online and in its stores, with a few exceptions, including some carrier-financed iPhones and iPads.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/11/apple-logo-holiday-feature.jpg" alt="" width="1920" height="1080" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1076074" /><br/>
In the U.S., Canada, the U.K., Ireland, Germany, the Netherlands, Australia, New Zealand, Singapore, and many other countries, most products purchased between November 6 and December 25 of this year may be returned through January 8, 2027, <a href="https://www.apple.com/shop/help/returns_refund">according to Apple's website</a>. All purchases made after December 25 in those countries are subject to Apple's standard 14-day return policy (15 days in Canada).<br/>
<br/>
For online orders, Apple says products "received" on November 6 through December 25 are eligible for return through January 8.<br/>
<br/>
In some countries, such as Mexico, Italy, Spain, and Japan, the return window is slightly longer. Apple says eligible products purchased in those countries between November 6 and January 6, 2027 may be returned through January 20, 2027.<br/>
<br/>
This policy applies to purchases at Apple Stores, on Apple.com, and in the Apple Store app.<br/>
<br/>
